// §10 third-party schema survey — SpiceDB's own Schema Language
// Reference, "typechecking" example. Source (fetched verbatim):
// https://raw.githubusercontent.com/authzed/docs/main/app/spicedb/concepts/schema/page.mdx
//
// Direct translation. The docs themselves call this out as a real
// authoring bug the schema language's own `use typechecking` directive
// exists to catch at write-schema time: "a call to CheckPermission for
// document#edit will _always_ return false at runtime because no
// relationship can simultaneously be for a user subject and for a
// serviceaccount subject." This survey checks that exact claim from the
// other direction — statically, not just "at runtime."

namespace document {
  relation viewer: user
  relation admin: serviceaccount

  permission edit = viewer & admin
}
